<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>unbatch — reconciliation report (seed {{ seed }})</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #f5f6fa;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --border: #e1e4ea;
    --text: #171923;
    --text-muted: #5b6472;
    --accent: #2453d6;
    --accent-soft: #eaf0fe;
    --good: #157a45;
    --good-soft: #e7f6ee;
    --bad: #b3261e;
    --bad-soft: #fbeaea;
    --warn: #9a6400;
    --warn-soft: #fdf3e0;
    --neutral-soft: #eef0f4;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font: 16px/1.55 -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page {
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px 32px 80px;
  }
  header.hero {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  header.hero h1 {
    font-size: 30px;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  header.hero p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 28px 32px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(16, 24, 40, 0.04);
  }
  .card h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .card h3 {
    font-size: 16px;
    margin: 22px 0 10px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  th, td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 9px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  th { color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 600; font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; }
  td.metric-name { color: var(--text-muted); white-space: normal; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .pending { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .pill {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 2px 10px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .pill-good { background: var(--good-soft); color: var(--good); }
  .pill-bad { background: var(--bad-soft); color: var(--bad); }
  .pill-warn { background: var(--warn-soft); color: var(--warn); }
  .pill-neutral { background: var(--neutral-soft); color: var(--text-muted); }
  .callout {
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .callout-info { background: var(--accent-soft); color: #163a91; }
  .callout-warn { background: var(--warn-soft); color: #6b4a00; }
  .callout-bad { background: var(--bad-soft); color: #7a1c17; }
  .callout strong { font-weight: 700; }
  .arm-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .arm-summary {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .arm-summary h3 { margin-top: 0; }
  .arm-summary .headline { font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; margin: 4px 0 2px; }
  .arm-summary .sub { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .funnel-rows { margin: 10px 0; }
  .funnel-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin: 5px 0; }
  .funnel-row-label {
    width: 26px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .funnel-row-track {
    flex: 1;
    background: var(--neutral-soft);
    border-radius: 5px;
    height: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .funnel-row-fill { height: 100%; min-width: 3px; border-radius: 5px; }
  .funnel-row-count {
    width: 70px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    text-align: right;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .hist { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: 4px; height: 120px; margin: 12px 0 4px; }
  .hist-bar { flex: 1; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0; min-height: 2px; }
  .hist-labels { display: flex; gap: 4px; font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .hist-labels span { flex: 1; text-align: center; }
  .diag { background: var(--good-soft) !important; font-weight: 700; }
  .off-diag-nonzero { background: var(--bad-soft) !important; }
  code { background: var(--neutral-soft); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 13px; }
  .section-note { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 14px; margin: 6px 0 0; }
  td.rationale-cell { white-space: normal; max-width: 420px; overflow-wrap: break-word; }
  footer { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; text-align: center; margin-top: 40px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">

  <header class="hero">
    <h1>unbatch — settlement reconciliation report</h1>
    <p>seed {{ seed }} · generated by <code>unbatch report</code> from out/audit.db · every number below is produced by <code>metrics.py</code>, nothing hand-entered</p>
  </header>

  <!-- ============ HEADLINE ============ -->
  <section class="card">
    <h2>Result, at a glance <span class="pill pill-neutral">arm B — rules + LLM</span></h2>
    {% if arms.with_llm.ran %}
    {% set m = arms.with_llm.metrics %}
    <div class="arm-grid">
      <div class="arm-summary">
        <h3>Total credits</h3>
        <div class="headline">{{ m.total_credits }}</div>
        <div class="sub">seed {{ seed }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="arm-summary">
        <h3>Match rate</h3>
        <div class="headline">{{ m.count_match_rate | percent }}</div>
        <div class="sub">{{ (m.count_match_rate * m.total_credits) | round | int }} of {{ m.total_credits }} resolved</div>
      </div>
      <div class="arm-summary">
        <h3>False-match rate</h3>
        <div class="headline">{{ m.false_match_rate | percent }}</div>
        <div class="sub">{{ "zero false matches" if m.false_match_rate == 0 else "not zero — see below" }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="arm-summary">
        <h3>Exceptions</h3>
        <div class="headline">{{ m.exception_rate | percent }}</div>
        <div class="sub">{{ (m.exception_rate * m.total_credits) | round | int }} credits, unresolved</div>
      </div>
      <div class="arm-summary">
        <h3>Total LLM cost</h3>
        <div class="headline">{{ arms.with_llm.llm_cost_rupees }}</div>
        <div class="sub">{{ m.llm_call_count }} calls</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <p class="pending">Arm B (rules + LLM) has not been run yet — run <code>unbatch demo</code>, or <code>unbatch run --cached</code> then <code>unbatch report</code>, to populate this summary.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- ============ ABLATION COMPARISON ============ -->
  <section class="card">
    <h2>Ablation — rules only vs. rules + LLM vs. LLM only</h2>

    {% if delta_b_minus_a is not none %}
    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <strong>Value the AI added to match rate (B − A): {{ (delta_b_minus_a * 100) | round(1) }} points</strong>
      ({{ arms.no_llm.metrics.count_match_rate | percent }} → {{ arms.with_llm.metrics.count_match_rate | percent }}).
      {% if delta_b_minus_a * 100 < 3 %}This is small, and reported as such — see the framing below for why that is the expected result here, not a disappointment.{% endif %}
      {% if arms.with_llm.has_llm_calls %}
      <strong>What the delta doesn't show:</strong> break-reason accuracy on arm B is {{ arms.with_llm.metrics.break_reason_accuracy | percent }} —
      a separate signal, additional to the match-rate delta above. Match rate only scores whether a credit resolved and to what payment_ids;
      it cannot see whether the model correctly explained <em>why</em> a break happened for the credits it touches, which is the actual job
      L4 exists to do. A high break-reason accuracy alongside a small match-rate delta is a real, specific capability, not a consolation prize
      for a small delta — see METRICS.md's own section on this.
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <div class="callout callout-warn">
      <strong>Arm B (rules + LLM) has not been run yet</strong> — the B − A delta needs a live run of <code>unbatch run</code> (or <code>--cached</code> once cache/ is populated) before it can be reported.
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if framing %}
    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <strong>Reading the exception count correctly:</strong> of the {{ framing.total_exceptions }} credits reaching L4 in arm A,
      {{ framing.correctly_declined }} are cases the rules layer <strong>correctly declined</strong> —
      {{ framing.ambiguous_composition }} <code>ambiguous_composition</code> (two valid payment-line subsets compose the same amount)
      and {{ framing.tolerance_ambiguous }} <code>tolerance_ambiguous</code> (two settlement batches both land inside the tolerance band) —
      plus {{ framing.unrelated_credit }} <code>unrelated_credit</code> with nothing to tie to at all.
      {% if framing.other > 0 %}Only {{ framing.other }} of the {{ framing.total_exceptions }} are cases rules alone could plausibly have resolved with more information.{% else %}None of the {{ framing.total_exceptions }} are cases rules alone could ever resolve — every one needs judgment, not more rules.{% endif %}
      The model's job on these is <strong>classifying why the break happened</strong>, not rescuing a match — a small or near-zero match-rate delta is the correct outcome here, not a disappointing one.
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if arms.with_llm.ran and arms.with_llm.metrics.false_match_rate > 0 %}
    <div class="callout callout-bad">
      <strong>Arm B false-match rate is {{ arms.with_llm.metrics.false_match_rate | percent }}, not zero.</strong>
      If the adjudicator confidently matched an <code>ambiguous_composition</code> or <code>tolerance_ambiguous</code> credit to one of its two
      valid-looking candidates, that is a false match by ground truth's definition even at high model confidence — see the exception/match
      table for arm B below for exactly which credits.
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Metric</th>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<th>{{ arms[arm].label }}<br><span class="pending">{{ arms[arm].command }}</span></th>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Count match rate</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.count_match_rate | percent }}{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Value-weighted match rate</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.value_weighted_match_rate | percent }}{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">False-match rate</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}<span class="{{ 'pill pill-bad' if arms[arm].metrics.false_match_rate > 0 else 'pill pill-good' }}">{{ arms[arm].metrics.false_match_rate | percent }}</span>{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Exception rate</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.exception_rate | percent }}{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Precision</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.precision | percent }}{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Recall (excludes correctly-unresolvable)</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.recall | percent }}{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Correctly rejected</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.correctly_rejected }}{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Break-reason accuracy</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran and arms[arm].has_llm_calls %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.break_reason_accuracy | percent }} <span class="pending">(n={{ arms[arm].classified_count }})</span>{% elif arms[arm].ran %}<span class="pending">N/A — no LLM calls</span>{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">LLM call count</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.llm_call_count }} / {{ arms[arm].metrics.total_credits }} ({{ arms[arm].metrics.llm_call_rate | percent }}){% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">LLM cost</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].llm_cost_rupees }}{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Cost per adjudicated credit</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran and arms[arm].has_llm_calls %}{{ arms[arm].cost_per_adjudicated_credit_paise }} paise{% elif arms[arm].ran %}<span class="pending">N/A — no LLM calls</span>{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Cost per exception surfaced</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran and arms[arm].metrics.exception_rate > 0 %}{{ arms[arm].cost_per_exception_paise }} paise{% elif arms[arm].ran %}<span class="pending">N/A — no exceptions</span>{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Malformed JSON responses</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.malformed_json_count }}{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Retries</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.retry_count }}{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Adjudication failed</td>
          {% for arm in arm_order %}<td>{% if arms[arm].ran %}{{ arms[arm].metrics.adjudication_failed_count }}{% else %}<span class="pending">not yet run</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    {% if arms.llm_only.ran and arms.with_llm.ran %}
    <p class="section-note">
      Arm C made {{ arms.llm_only.metrics.llm_call_count }} LLM calls against arm B's {{ arms.with_llm.metrics.llm_call_count }}
      ({{ (arms.llm_only.metrics.llm_call_count / arms.with_llm.metrics.llm_call_count) | round(1) }}× as many, since it skips the rules layers that would have resolved most credits for free)
      for a {{ ((arms.with_llm.metrics.count_match_rate - arms.llm_only.metrics.count_match_rate) * 100) | round(1) }}-point <em>worse</em> match rate
      ({{ arms.llm_only.metrics.count_match_rate | percent }} vs. arm B's {{ arms.with_llm.metrics.count_match_rate | percent }})
      and a {{ ((arms.with_llm.metrics.break_reason_accuracy - arms.llm_only.metrics.break_reason_accuracy) * 100) | round(1) }}-point worse break-reason accuracy
      ({{ arms.llm_only.metrics.break_reason_accuracy | percent }} vs. arm B's {{ arms.with_llm.metrics.break_reason_accuracy | percent }}) —
      that gap, not the rupee total (both arms are cheap in absolute terms), is the evidence for the cascade's design, not a bug in arm C.
      {% set fm_b = arms.with_llm.metrics.false_match_rate %}
      {% set fm_c = arms.llm_only.metrics.false_match_rate %}
      {% if fm_b == 0 and fm_c == 0 %}
      Notably, false-match rate stayed at 0% in {% if arms.no_llm.ran %}all three arms{% else %}both arm B and arm C{% endif %}: even with no rules help at all, the model did not confidently commit to a wrong match — it just resolved far less.
      {% else %}
      Notably, false-match rate did <em>not</em> stay at 0% here: arm C's is {{ fm_c | percent }}{% if arms.no_llm.ran %}, against arm A's {{ arms.no_llm.metrics.false_match_rate | percent }} and arm B's {{ fm_b | percent }}{% else %}, against arm B's {{ fm_b | percent }}{% endif %}. Without the rules layers narrowing the candidate set first, the model can confidently attach a credit to the wrong nearby batch — see FAILURES.md's entry on the first false match this project measured for the mechanism.
      {% endif %}
    </p>
    {% else %}
    <p class="section-note">Arm C (LLM only) is expected to score worse than arm A at many times the LLM call volume — that is the evidence for the cascade's design, not a bug in arm C.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% set mf_b = arms.with_llm.metrics.malformed_json_count if arms.with_llm.ran else none %}
    {% set mf_c = arms.llm_only.metrics.malformed_json_count if arms.llm_only.ran else none %}
    {% if mf_b is not none or mf_c is not none %}
      {% if not mf_b and not mf_c %}
    <p class="section-note">A zero malformed-JSON count on the LLM arms reflects OpenAI's schema-enforced structured output (<code>response_format</code> strict JSON Schema against <code>AdjudicationResult</code>'s own shape) actually working, not an absent check — the retry-then-degrade path (see <code>adjudicator.py</code>) still runs on every call and would catch a refusal or truncated response if one occurred; see <code>test_adjudicator.py</code>'s retry-path tests for the exercised failure modes.</p>
      {% else %}
    <p class="section-note">
      <strong>Malformed-JSON responses:</strong> {% if mf_b %}arm B saw {{ mf_b }}{% endif %}{% if mf_b and mf_c %}; {% endif %}{% if mf_c %}arm C saw {{ mf_c }}{% endif %}.
      OpenAI's schema-enforced structured output (<code>response_format</code> strict JSON Schema) still passed on every one of these — the JSON itself was well-formed. What failed was semantic validation: <code>adjudicator.py</code> checks that the model's cited <code>evidence_refs</code> actually reference a record it was shown, and rejected these for citing something outside that set, then retried once before degrading. This is the evidence-grounding gap documented in FAILURES.md, not a JSON parsing failure.
    </p>
      {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <!-- ============ PER-ARM DETAIL ============ -->
  {% for arm in arm_order %}
  {% set view = arms[arm] %}
  <section class="card">
    <h2>{{ view.label }} <span class="pill pill-neutral">{{ view.command }}</span></h2>

    {% if not view.ran %}
      <p class="pending">This arm has not been run against this seed yet — run <code>{{ view.command }}</code> (add <code>--cached</code> once cache/ is populated, or <code>--confirm-spend</code> for a live <code>--llm-only</code> run) then regenerate this report.</p>
    {% else %}
      <p class="section-note">run_id <code>{{ view.run_id }}</code></p>

      <h3>Stage funnel</h3>
      {% set stage_colors = {'l0': '#2453d6', 'l1': '#4f7ad9', 'l2': '#7c98de', 'l3': '#9a6400', 'l4': '#b3261e'} %}
      <div class="funnel-rows">
        {% for row in view.funnel_rows %}
        <div class="funnel-row">
          <span class="funnel-row-label">{{ row.stage }}</span>
          <div class="funnel-row-track">
            <div class="funnel-row-fill" style="width: {{ row.percent_of_total }}%; background: {{ stage_colors.get(row.stage, '#8a94a6') }};"></div>
          </div>
          <span class="funnel-row-count">{{ row.count }} resolved</span>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      {% if view.confusion_table %}
      <h3>Break-reason confusion — ground truth (rows) vs. model prediction (columns)</h3>
      <p class="section-note">n = {{ view.classified_count }} classified credits (of {{ view.metrics.llm_call_count }} LLM calls; {{ view.metrics.adjudication_failed_count }} degraded to <code>adjudication_failed</code> and are excluded here, see the exception note below). A sample this small should be read as directional, not precise.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Ground truth ↓ / Predicted →</th>{% for col in view.confusion_table.columns %}<th>{{ col }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for actual, cells in view.confusion_table.rows %}
          <tr>
            <td class="metric-name">{{ actual }}</td>
            {% for col in view.confusion_table.columns %}
              {% set count = cells[loop.index0] %}
              <td class="{% if col == actual and count > 0 %}diag{% elif col != actual and count > 0 %}off-diag-nonzero{% endif %}">{{ count }}</td>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>
      <p class="section-note">Green = correct classification. Red = a break_reason that does not match ground truth's break_type.</p>
      {% elif view.has_llm_calls %}
      <p class="section-note">No successful classifications to show a confusion table for (every LLM call degraded to <code>adjudication_failed</code>).</p>
      {% else %}
      <p class="section-note">This arm made no LLM calls, so there is no break-reason accuracy to report.</p>
      {% endif %}

      <h3>Confidence distribution (adjudicator decisions only)</h3>
      {% if view.has_llm_calls %}
      <p class="section-note">L0-L3's confidences are fixed constants (1.00/0.98/0.90/0.75), so they are excluded here — this shows only the {{ view.metrics.llm_call_count }} decisions where confidence is a genuine model-reported value.</p>
      <div class="hist">
        {% for label, count in view.confidence_histogram %}
        <div class="hist-bar" style="height: {{ (count / view.confidence_histogram_max * 100) if view.confidence_histogram_max else 0 }}%;" title="{{ label }}: {{ count }} decisions"></div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="hist-labels">
        {% for label, count in view.confidence_histogram %}<span>{{ label }}</span>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% else %}
      <p class="section-note">This arm never calls the adjudicator, so there is no model-reported confidence to plot.</p>
      {% endif %}

      <h3>Exceptions ({{ view.exceptions | length }} of {{ view.metrics.total_credits }}, full list, no truncation)</h3>
      {% if view.metrics.adjudication_failed_count > 0 %}
      <p class="section-note">
        <strong>{{ view.metrics.adjudication_failed_count }} of these are <code>adjudication_failed</code></strong>, shown below with a blank rationale: the model's response failed validation twice in a row (the first attempt, then a retry with the validation error appended) and never produced a usable classification, so there is nothing to show in place of one. On seed 42 this is semantic validation rejecting the response for citing evidence outside what the model was actually shown, not a crash or a timeout — see FAILURES.md's evidence-grounding-gap entry.
      </p>
      {% endif %}
      {% if view.exceptions %}
      <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Credit</th><th>Stage</th><th>Reason</th><th>Confidence</th><th>Delta</th><th>Rationale</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for row in view.exceptions %}
          <tr>
            <td><code>{{ row.credit_id }}</code></td>
            <td>{{ row.stage }}</td>
            <td>{{ row.reason }}</td>
            <td>{{ row.confidence | percent }}</td>
            <td>{{ row.delta_rupees }}</td>
            <td class="rationale-cell">{{ row.rationale or "—" }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>
      {% else %}
      <p class="section-note">No exceptions in this arm — every credit resolved (check the false-match rate above before reading that as a win).</p>
      {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  <!-- ============ FORWARD CASH FORECAST ============ -->
  {% if forecast %}
  <section class="card">
    <h2>Forward cash forecast <span class="pill pill-neutral">unbatch forecast --horizon {{ forecast.horizon_days }}</span></h2>
    <p class="section-note">A separate loop from reconciliation above, over the same settlement report — see forecast.py's module docstring. Pure arithmetic, no LLM: fits a settlement-lag mode and a fee-schedule deviation stdev on data settled on or before <code>{{ forecast.as_of }}</code> ({{ forecast.historical_payment_count }} historical payments), then projects every order captured by then but still unsettled ({{ forecast.unsettled_payment_count }} of them) onto its expected settlement day.</p>

    <div class="callout callout-bad">
      <strong>Measured limitation, not a bug:</strong> with this gateway's 1-2 day settlement lag, an order that is still unsettled as of <code>{{ forecast.as_of }}</code> is either on schedule to settle the very next day or already overdue — there is no way for an already-captured order to honestly project onto day 3, day 7, or day 14. The six-seed backtest (bench_forecast.json) found this population accounts for roughly <strong>10% of actual 14-day inflow</strong> on average; the rest comes from orders not yet captured as of the forecast date, which no projection over settlement data alone can see. Reported plainly rather than dressed up — see ARCHITECTURE.md's forecasting operating envelope.
    </div>

    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>&nbsp;</th><th>Expected</th><th>Low</th><th>High</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="metric-name">Total over {{ forecast.horizon_days }} days</td>
          <td>{{ forecast.total_expected_rupees }}</td>
          <td>{{ forecast.total_low_rupees }}</td>
          <td>{{ forecast.total_high_rupees }}</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Daily breakdown</h3>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Expected</th><th>Low</th><th>High</th><th>Payments</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for day in forecast.daily %}
        <tr>
          <td>{{ day.date }}</td>
          <td>{{ day.expected_rupees }}</td>
          <td>{{ day.low_rupees }}</td>
          <td>{{ day.high_rupees }}</td>
          <td>{{ day.payment_count }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p class="section-note">Band width comes from the observed deviation between actual settled nets and what fees.py's own fee schedule would compute (stdev {{ (forecast.historical_deviation_stdev * 100) | round(3) }}% of gross on this fit window) — narrow, because the fee schedule is deterministic and only genuine drift (a fee-tier change, a refund/chargeback risk) shows up here at all.</p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <footer>unbatch — Razorpay AI Buildathon, Track 04. Generated from out/audit.db; every figure traces to a line in metrics.py.</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
